---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import simpsons from './assets/simpsons-rollercoaster.jpg';
import previousWebsite from './assets/previous-website.png';
import currentWebsite from './assets/current-website.png';
import vocaberWords from './assets/vocaber-words.png';
import vocaberReview from './assets/vocaber-review.png';
import impeccableExample from './assets/impeccable-2026.png';
import metadata from './metadata';
---
<ArticleLayout metadata={metadata} showDescription={false}>
  <p>As someone working in a field being heavily disrupted by AI —<sup><a id="em-dash-ref" href="#em-dash-note"
      aria-label="Footnote 1">1</a></sup> software development — I’m constantly torn about the subject.</p>

  <p>On one hand, it’s been a huge enabler. I’m able to be much more ambitious with
    projects and ship them faster. I’ve been able to build, and build well, personal
    projects I’d always wanted to start but never had the time for.</p>

  <p>But on the other hand, it’s brought a lot of uncertainty to software and many other professions. 
    Not to mention the moral grey area of how these models were trained (Grand Theft Autocomplete..), 
    the immense resources they take to run, the impact of companies trying to jam AI data centres into every community 
    and the daunting economic "is-it is-it-not a bubble" in play.</p>

  <p>A daily rollercoaster of emotions is what it is.</p>

  <figure class="post-image">
    <Image src={simpsons}
      widths={[480, 896, 1792, 2000]}
      sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 50.4rem, 84vw"
      alt="Homer Simpson cycling through three emotions, captioned: The terrifying lows, the dizzying highs, the creamy middles."
      loading="lazy" />
  </figure>

  <p>But it’s official: AI has finally gone too far and must be stopped.</p>

  <p>It has ruined neo-brutalism.</p>

  <p><a href="https://www.nngroup.com/articles/neobrutalism/">Neo-brutalism</a>{' '}
    is a design style I’ve been a big fan for years, especially the softer versions with charcoal
    and pastels.</p>

  <p>The previous version of this website, built in 2021, used this style.</p>

  <figure class="post-image screenshot-figure">
    <a class="screenshot-link" href={previousWebsite.src} aria-label="View the full-size previous website screenshot">
      <Image src={previousWebsite}
        format="png"
        widths={[480, 672, 1008, 1344]}
        sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 42rem, 84vw"
        alt="The top half of the previous Barnaby Bishop website, with a portrait beside the heading and mint and blue content panels with hard charcoal shadows."
        loading="lazy" />
    </a>
  </figure>

  <p>When building an app to help me learn Korean, I used it again…</p>

  <figure class="post-image screenshot-figure screenshot-pair" aria-label="Vocaber app screenshots">
    <a class="screenshot-link" href={vocaberWords.src} aria-label="View the full-size Vocaber word list screenshot">
      <Image src={vocaberWords}
        widths={[240, 360, 720, 1170]}
        sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 20rem, 41vw"
        alt="Vocaber’s Korean vocabulary list, with English translations, pastel proficiency badges and a rounded bottom navigation bar."
        loading="lazy" />
    </a>
    <a class="screenshot-link" href={vocaberReview.src} aria-label="View the full-size Vocaber flashcard screenshot">
      <Image src={vocaberReview}
        widths={[240, 360, 720, 1170]}
        sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 20rem, 41vw"
        alt="Vocaber’s review screen showing a flashcard for 닮다, meaning to resemble or be alike, with an example sentence and a solid charcoal shadow."
        loading="lazy" />
    </a>
  </figure>

  <p>My Korean still sucks, but the app is very visually pleasing to use.</p>

  <p>When redesigning this website I wanted to combine the '80s-90s Memphis design style shapes and colours
    with a bit of neo-brutalism. They’re a match made in heaven!</p>

  <figure class="post-image screenshot-figure">
    <a class="screenshot-link" href={currentWebsite.src} aria-label="View the full-size website screenshot at launch">
      <Image src={currentWebsite}
        format="png"
        widths={[480, 672, 1008, 1344]}
        sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 42rem, 84vw"
        alt="The redesigned Barnaby Bishop homepage, with a teal nameplate, colourful Memphis shapes and both launch posts dated 21 and 19 November 2026."
        loading="lazy" />
    </a>
    <figcaption>The site design at launch. It has probably changed by now.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>So you can imagine my dismay when, on the eve of pushing this redesign live,
    fellow Thinkmiller <a href="https://dineshpandiyan.com/">Dinesh</a> shared{' '}
    <a href="https://impeccable.style/">Impeccable</a> with me: a set of skills to help agents with design.</p>

  <p>There, among its <a href="https://impeccable.style/slop/">examples of 2026 AI
    design slop</a>, was neo-brutalism.</p>

  <p>Cry.</p>

  <figure class="post-image screenshot-figure">
    <a class="screenshot-link" href={impeccableExample.src} aria-label="View the full-size Impeccable 2026 example screenshot">
      <Image src={impeccableExample}
        format="png"
        widths={[480, 672, 1008, 1344]}
        sizes="(min-width: 60.4rem) 42rem, 84vw"
        alt="Impeccable’s Slop heading above its selected 2026 example: a yellow neo-brutalist website annotated for hard offset shadows and nested cards."
        loading="lazy" />
    </a>
    <figcaption><a href="https://impeccable.style/slop/">Impeccable’s 2026 AI design slop example.</a></figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>Too far AI, too far.</p>

  <section slot="footnotes" class="footnotes" aria-label="Footnotes">
    <ol>
      <li id="em-dash-note">
        <p>Enjoy this artisanally hand-typed em dash. I had to look up how to do it (option + shift + "-" on mac ).{' '}
          <a href="#em-dash-ref" aria-label="Back to footnote 1 reference">↩</a></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  .post-image {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 60.4rem) {
    .screenshot-figure {
      margin-inline: 8%;
    }
  }

  .post-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }

  .screenshot-link {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--color-ink);
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }

  .screenshot-link img { border-radius: 0; }

  .screenshot-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: start;
    gap: clamp(.75rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  sup {
    font-size: .7em;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  sup a { padding-inline: .15em; }

  .footnotes {
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .footnotes ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.5em;
  }

  .footnotes p { margin: 0; }
  .footnotes li { scroll-margin-top: var(--space-4); }
</style>
